I've inspected the wiki entry[*] about role difficulty; the rationale for
the approach (cf. link) looks a bit suspect to me[**], and the ranking of
one specific entry (the "Arc") looks anyway very strange to me. (Fourth
easiest class, really?)

So I've done my own statistics[***], considering games of players with
at least 13 ascensions and an ascension ratio of at least 2%, and whose
games have a standard deviation of at most 0.20 (i.e. excluding players
who focus on few roles only). I've grouped the players in four classes
w.r.t. ascension ratio (A: 50-100%, B: 25-50%, C: 10-25%, and D: 2-10%),
and in four classes w.r.t. randomness of played classes (<0.10, <0.12,
<0.16, and <0.20, bisased towards the more random distributed games).

I've grouped the rank results by the ascension class A-D (see above),
and built an overall ranking from those (the wiki data can be found for
comparison in the last column)...

 rank overall   A    B    C    D    (Wiki)
   1.   Val    Sam  Val  Bar  Val     Val
   2.   Bar    Val  Cav  Val  Sam     Bar
   3.   Sam    Bar  Bar  Sam  Bar     Sam
   4.   Cav    Ran  Ran  Kni  Kni     Arc
   5.   Kni    Cav  Sam  Hea  Cav     Cav
   6.   Ran    Wiz  Hea  Pri  Tou     Mon
   7.   Hea    Mon  Kni  Cav  Mon     Ran
   8.   Mon    Hea  Mon /Mon  Hea     Kni
   9.   Pri    Kni  Rog \Tou  Ran     Hea
  10.   Tou   /Pri  Arc  Ran  Pri     Pri
  11.   Rog   \Rog  Pri  Rog  Rog     Wiz
  12.   Wiz   /Tou  Tou  Wiz  Wiz     Rog
  13.   Arc   \Arc  Wiz  Arc  Arc     Tou

Note: braces around pairs of entried denote equal metric values of those
entries.

As expected, there are slight variances depending on ascension class A-D,
and the basic well known picture about easy classes matches. But there's
one obvious difference (compared to the approach in the Wiki); the "Arc"
is on rank 4 (forth easiest, according to the Wiki approach) or rank 13
(most difficult, according to my approach). Any opinions where that good
ranking of Archeologists comes from? Is it justifiable?

